    "highlights": "1. Negative letter-spacing scaling: Larger display headings aggressively tighten their letter-spacing (from -0.01em to -0.12rem) to maintain visual density, while body text rests at 0em.\n2. Eyebrow treatments: Ultra-small uppercase UI text (0.625rem - 0.6875rem) paired with wide tracking (0.075rem - 0.103rem) and medium weight (550) for maximal legibility at micro sizes.",
    "insights": [
      "The system leverages a variable font (Instrument Sans) to implement an unusually precise weight scale, utilizing 450 for 'normal' and 550 for 'medium', optimizing optical weight without the bulk of standard 500/600 values.",
      "Typographic tokens are rigidly structured using a CSS variable system that maps roles (e.g., 'display', 'headline', 'body-long') to specific size, line-height, and tracking combinations, ensuring layout stability.",
      "Lab color spaces are deeply integrated with the typography scale for foreground elements, pointing to a highly calibrated contrast and theming strategy."
